Commit:     c1a00002 Executive <executive@viche.local>
CommitDate: Sat Nov 7 14:35:37 2026 +0000

    Gate case closure on case-bound independent verification artifacts
    
    The previous commit treated producer observed_at values as independent health
    observations. An independent review showed those producers (branch-liveness,
    outcome-metrics, judiciary-measurements, innovation cycles) re-stamp
    observed_at every boot cycle even when nothing changed, so that scheme was a
    re-stamped heartbeat, not independent evidence. It also allowed key-set
    substitution, out-of-order rows, and non-binding evidence tokens.
    
    Revert that generation scheme entirely: branch-health rows go back to
    timestamp<TAB>signals. Healthy probe rows are now an explicit PRECONDITION
    only.
    
    Closure now requires a case-bound independent verification artifact at
    <state>/verification/<signal>.json:
      * case_id must equal the case id, so an artifact cannot be reused for a later
        case of the same signal;
      * verified_by must be an independent office (judiciary or clerk), never the
        Executive that owns the repair;
      * verified_at must be later than the case first_seen (no pre-dated artifact);
      * evidence.ref must resolve to a durable file whose sha256 matches the
        recorded digest, so the claim is checkable and tamper-evident.
    
    Continuity cases additionally still require their validated reconciliation
    receipt. When healthy probes reach two but no valid artifact exists, the case
    stays open with awaiting_independent_verification=true, so the gap is visible
    and routed rather than silently closed.
    
    Tests now drive the production branch-health script through repeated
    identical-state cycles and assert: no closure without an artifact; wrong case
    id, non-independent verifier, pre-dated artifact, missing evidence, bad digest
    and artifact reuse are all refused; a valid artifact closes exactly once.

